:"Colorado Buffaloes players says the return of head coach Deion Sanders following his recent battle with bladder cancer has been \"a breath of fresh air.\"","published":"2025-08-01T11:45:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/45862667/deion-sanders-return-breath-fresh-air-colorado-players","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Purdue rolls with FAA ground stop by taking buses to Iowa","description":"Unable to travel by plane, the Boilermakers rolled with the situation and found some good times on the way.","published":"2026-11-17T11:28:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504665/purdue-faa-ground-stop-bus-iowa","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Heisman of Week 11: Duke's Nate Sheppard has entered the running","description":"In a season in which star running backs seem to be popping up out of nowhere, the Blue Devils' sophomore stands out.","published":"2026-11-17T11:35:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503621/heisman-watch-week-11-duke-nate-sheppard","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on College Football Playoff bubble ahead of committee's third ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-17T11:24:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503628/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-third-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Breaking down the major futures for the Big Ten, from the Heisman to the CFP","description":"Let's evaluate whether a standout performance on a three-loss team and a 10-0 team are real or a mirage in the Big Ten.","published":"2026-11-17T13:02:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50504671/college-football-heisman-trophy-cfp-futures-betting-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Arkansas State tells Butch Jones he's out at end of year","description":"Arkansas State has informed football coach Butch Jones that he's out at the end of the season, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Monday night.","published":"2026-11-17T02:45:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50506952/sources-butch-jones-arkansas-state-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-16T23:15:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Illinois may turn to third-string QB Boyd after Houser injury","description":"Illinois might turn to third-string quarterback Carson Boyd this week against No. 15 Iowa after starter Katin Houser suffered a broken nose Friday at UCLA that required surgery.","published":"2026-11-16T21:42:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504718/illinois-turn-third-string-qb-boyd-houser-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rivers says NC State only college job he would have taken","description":"New coach Philip Rivers said NC State was the only college job he would have taken.","published":"2026-11-17T12:34:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504530/rivers-says-nc-state-only-college-job-taken","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4707184/dj-mckinney","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJ_McKinney"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"DJ McKinney","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJ_McKinney","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:46Z","intro":"Dylahn Jordan McKinney (born February 9, 2004) is an American college football cornerback for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously played for the Oklahoma State Cowboys and Colorado Buffaloes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McKinney attended Colleyville Heritage High School in Colleyville, Texas. He had 43 tackles and two interceptions his junior year and 35 tackles and five interceptions as a senior. He committed to Oklahoma State University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"McKinney played at Oklahoma State in 2022 and 2023. After redshirting his first year in 2022, he played in all 14 games in 2023 and had 38 tackles. After the season, McKinney entered the transfer portal and transferred to the University of Colorado Boulder. In his first year at Colorado in 2024, he started all 13 games and had 62 tackles, three interceptions and one interception returned for a touchdown. McKinney returned in 2025, where he played nine games and had 35 tackles, one interception, and five pass breakups. At the end of the season, McKinney entered the transfer portal and transferred to Notre Dame."}]}}